# Full release steps: see portal/DEPLOY.txt and scripts/build-portal.sh
#
# Option C: deploy the Vite app on a separate origin (e.g. https://support.customer.com)
# and point API calls at your Frappe / ERPNext site.
#
# VITE_FRAPPE_SITE_URL=https://erp.yourcompany.com
#
# Site config (site_config.json or common_site_config.json) must include the portal origin, e.g.:
# "allow_cors": ["https://support.customer.com"]
#
# Sign-in is handled inside the portal (portal_login API). Session cookies are set on the bench host;
# allow_cors + credentials are required for cross-origin requests.
#
# Local UI demo: load fixtures from portal/src/portalMock.ts (no login, no API).
# To turn OFF mock: set VITE_PORTAL_USE_MOCK_DATA=false (or delete the line), restart `npm run dev`,
# run `npm run build` again for production, and hard-refresh the browser. Optional: add ?mock=0 once
# to clear an old session flag, or use VITE_PORTAL_USE_MOCK_DATA=false which clears it automatically.
# VITE_PORTAL_USE_MOCK_DATA=true
#
# Built assets do not read .env at runtime — the bundle embeds VITE_* at build time.
